# Automatic submission defaults and explicit confirmation
Workstream-ID: lea-03
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/4
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: TODO.md, 2026-07-21 submit-default batch
Status: DONE
Milestone: Separate submission approval from unknown-answer prompting
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Track the completed change that made submission automatic by default while
retaining an explicit default-Yes terminal confirmation option.

## Tasks
- [x] Submit unless an explicit confirmation callback declines.
- [x] Provide `--confirm-submit` and `--no-confirm-submit`.
- [x] Make Enter approve an explicitly requested confirmation.
- [x] Keep unknown-question prompting independent from submission approval.
- [x] Preserve dry-run behavior and update command documentation.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Historical tests cover automatic, approved, declined and dry-run paths.
- [x] The old default-No prompt no longer silently discards on Enter.

## Completion evidence
The 2026-07-21 source records five submission-confirmation cases, a 169-test
green suite and clean Ruff/Black/mypy checks. Relevant implementations are
`EasyApplyWorkflow._finalize_submit` and CLI confirmation wiring.
DONE refers to this technical batch, not a guarantee of external submission.
User acceptance, external qualification and publication are not inferred.
This migration did not submit any applications.

## Completion log
- 2026-07-21: Submission-default implementation and documentation recorded complete.
